From c0e25abe4e3d48bac78c10b44d14ae547919f7f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:54:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 062/108] gpu: vulkan: resolve feed draws with the red/blue
 swap; Adreno-safe RT and shared memory barriers

- Resolve feed (vulkan_resolve_feed_textures, init-time, default off): a 1x
  k_8_8_8_8 resolve into an up-to-date cached R8G8B8A8 texture of the same
  format, endianness and pitch is drawn straight from the render target into
  the texture (fullscreen triangle, texelFetch, optional R/B swap for
  copy_dest_swap), so the texture stays valid instead of being reloaded.
  Fed textures get COLOR_ATTACHMENT usage. Shaders: glsl/resolve_feed.{vert,frag},
  built by scripts/shaders/build_host_rt_resolve_shaders.sh (spv_to_header.py).
- VulkanRenderTarget tracks its last write and the stages it was made visible
  to; barriers now take src_stage_mask(dst)/src_access_mask(dst), which add
  that write when the destination stages haven't seen it. Adreno doesn't
  honour dependency chains (write -> compute read -> fragment read): the feed
  read stale render target blocks without this.
- VulkanSharedMemory kComputeWrite used SHADER_READ as its access mask (as in
  Xenia), so barriers after resolves never made the resolve writes available.
- Diagnostics (default off): vulkan_resolve_feed_debug (magenta, all or one
  address), vulkan_resolve_feed_textures_no_mutable, vulkan_resolve_clear_full_barrier,
  vulkan_attachment_barrier_between_passes, gpu_debug_skip_transfers_mask,
  vulkan_gpu_trace_frames (trace N consecutive frames).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

